WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.885
Before your shift, check the Shared device label on
the Omni IC sign-in screen.

00:00:05.065 --> 00:00:07.540
Here it says Academy IC handoff desk.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.539
A named desk helps staff recognize the device they
are using.

00:00:11.719 --> 00:00:14.129
Sign in with your own account for your shift.

00:00:14.449 --> 00:00:18.993
Open Sign-in and security in Settings to check your
verification methods.

00:00:19.173 --> 00:00:23.056
This example has no authenticator app or passkeys
enrolled.

00:00:23.236 --> 00:00:29.743
If your department uses verification for shared
devices, confirm your setup before taking over a
desk.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:33.561
When you step away, find Session in Settings and
choose Lock.

00:00:33.741 --> 00:00:39.267
A desk shared by an industrial response team or
security shift can use the same control.

00:00:39.587 --> 00:00:42.232
The lock screen shows the signed-in operator.

00:00:42.412 --> 00:00:47.511
This training shift cannot be unlocked here because
the account has no eligible factor.

00:00:47.691 --> 00:00:49.931
Use End shift to return to sign-in.

00:00:50.111 --> 00:00:54.249
Use Switch operator when another authorized operator
is taking over.

00:00:54.569 --> 00:00:58.751
After End shift, the sign-in form returns with the
same device label.

00:00:58.931 --> 00:01:01.960
The next operator can start a shift with their own
account.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:07.153
This is useful at a search command post or a
community outreach coordination desk.
